      "creator" : {
         "accountId" : "557058:4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
         "accountType" : "atlassian",
         "active" : true,
         "avatarUrls" : {
            "16x16" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "24x24" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "32x32" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png",
            "48x48" : "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9415554eef74e2169ce3e459c177ff75?d=https%3A%2F%2Favatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net%2Finitials%2FLP-4.png"
         },
         "displayName" : "Lewis Pringle",
         "self" : "https://stroika.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3A4fe560ca-b4e1-41d1-9bdf-97b1684eda32",
         "timeZone" : "America/New_York"
      },
      "customfield_10001" : "1_*:*_1_*:*_305470097_*|*_5_*:*_1_*:*_0",
      "customfield_10012" : "0|i002w7:",
      "customfield_10300" : "{}",
      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Very hard bug I ran into with AIX, with stack overflow, triggered by a larger stack buffer in InputStream::ReadAll<byte> (I think).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Appears no standard way to ask total thread size or set total thread size, or total stack left. But all of these might be helpful.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Probably best thing todo is to provide API with STATIC DEFAULT (optional), and individual thread parametner (again optional). Use to specify stack on startup (just as part of creation).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Existing std::thread stack practice on differnt systems:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "Windows: calls _beginthreadex (stacksize=0) - which means use the default.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/ms686774%28v=vs.85%29.aspx?f=255&MSPPError=-2147217396"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://msdn.microsoft.com/en-us/library/windows/desktop/ms686774%28v=vs.85%29.aspx?f=255&MSPPError=-2147217396",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "he default size for the reserved and initially committed stack memory is specified in the executable file header. Thread or fiber creation fails if there is not enough memory to reserve or commit the number of bytes requested. The default stack reservation size used by the linker is 1 MB. To specify a different default stack reservation size for all threads and fibers, use the STACKSIZE statement in the module definition (.def) file. Not super easy to find stack size - but apparently you can somehow get tlb?? and from there get bacse and end of stack (so full size).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "GCC:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "Consider adding -fstack-protector or -fstack-protector-all to default gcc options for apply-debug-options. Verify that would have found the problme I an into with AIX.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "UNIX/Linux:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "gthread_create (_",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "em"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "gthread_t *threadid, void ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "strong"
                        },
                        {
                           "type" : "em"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "(",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "em"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "func) (void*),void *",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "_args)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "{ return _",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "type" : "em"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "gthrw",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "(pthread_create) (__threadid, NULL, __func, __args)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "so construcint std::thread wtih libstdc++ just uses the default for posix_threads.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "UNIX/AIX:",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "// According to ",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "marks" : [
                        {
                           "attrs" : {
                              "href" : "https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/ssw_aix_61/com.ibm.aix.performance/thread_supp_tun_params.htm"
                           },
                           "type" : "link"
                        }
                     ],
                     "text" : "https://www.ibm.com/support/knowledgecenter/ssw_aix_61/com.ibm.aix.performance/thread_supp_tun_params.htm",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "//      Default: 98 304 bytes for 32-bit applications, 196 608 bytes for 64-bit applications.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "//      Range: Decimal integer values from 0 to 268 435 455 which will be rounded up to the nearest page (currently 4 096).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "if (sizeof (void*) == 4)",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "{",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "static  const   char    kStackSizeEnvVarSetting_[]      =   \"AIXTHREAD_STK=130000\";",
                     "type" : "text"
                  },
                  {
                     "type" : "hardBreak"
                  },
                  {
                     "text" : "DbgTrace (\"Setting env-var %s\", kStackSizeEnvVarSetting_);",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
